PRACTICAL NO. 2 - WORKING WITH DATABASE / DATABASE HANDLING
============================================================
Aim
Handle database records in Python, export them, move them with NiFi, and automate extraction/loading with Airflow.

Basic concept
A relational database stores data in tables. A row is a record; a column is a field. PostgreSQL is the database in this practical. Elasticsearch is the destination used in the manual's NiFi/Airflow flows.

A. HANDLING DATABASE IN PYTHON

Requirements
PostgreSQL server, pgAdmin, Python packages psycopg2 (or psycopg2-binary), pandas and Faker. The manual names database dataengineering in the setup steps, while later examples use DE. Use one consistent database name and credentials.

Steps
