PRACTICAL NO. 3 - CLEANING, TRANSFORMING AND ENRICHING DATA
============================================================
Aim
Perform exploratory data analysis in Python, fix common data problems, create/modify columns, enrich data and automate cleaning with Airflow.

Basic concept
Cleaning makes data consistent and usable. Transformation changes its shape or values. Enrichment adds useful information or derived fields. EDA (exploratory data analysis) means inspecting a dataset before deciding what changes are needed.

A. EXPLORATORY DATA ANALYSIS IN PYTHON

Requirements
Python, pandas, and the source CSV used in the manual. The Airflow example uses scooter.csv with columns including region_id and started_at. The exact data values are not transcribed in the manual's text, so use the supplied class dataset.

Steps
1. Put the source CSV in your working folder and note the exact path.
2. Load it with pandas: df = pd.read_csv("yourfile.csv").
3. Inspect the first/last rows with df.head() and df.tail(), dimensions with df.shape, and fields/types with df.info().
4. Summarize numeric columns with df.describe(); inspect categories with df["column"].value_counts().
5. Check missing values with df.isna().sum() and duplicate rows with df.duplicated().sum().
6. Handle common data issues as required: drop an unwanted column with df.drop(columns=["column"]), drop rows with missing values with df.dropna(), or remove duplicates with df.drop_duplicates(). Always confirm the effect using df.shape.
7. Create/modify columns with direct assignment, string functions or date extraction; for example df["new_col"] = ... . Ensure date/time columns are parsed with pd.to_datetime before filtering.
8. Enrich data by adding a derived column, lookup value or other attribute relevant to the source. The manual has screenshots for these operations but does not transcribe every expression as text; use the actual column names and rule demonstrated in the supplied pages 17-22.
9. Save the cleaned/enriched result with df.to_csv("cleaned_data.csv", index=False).
10. Re-open the output file and verify the column names, row count and data types.

Useful EDA template (generic scaffolding, not a verbatim transcription of screenshot code)
