Aim
Configure Spark and PySpark, read CSV into a Spark DataFrame, display the schema and records, and apply DataFrame transformations and SQL.

Basic concept
Apache Spark is a distributed data-processing engine. PySpark lets you use Spark from Python. A DataFrame is a table-like object containing rows and columns. Spark can filter, select, group, aggregate and query large datasets.

Requirements
Java compatible with the Spark version, Python, Apache Spark archive, PySpark, CSV file named data.csv, and optional Jupyter Notebook/findspark for the final step. The manual's screenshots contain the sample data and setup paths; copy the same sample rows from page 92 of the supplied PDF if matching the classroom output matters.

